+ * backlight-marketing-table, the nits (16.16) at each slider step 0..100 %.
+ *
+ * A34 (1003): what 1002's boot showed, with CoreBrightness's code
+ * (CBDisplayModuleiOS, iOS 16.7): on a backlight like the iPhone X's it
+ * sets "brightness" and "backlight-level" = the level as a fraction B of
+ * IODisplayParameters' max (0..65536; with FadePeriod, DisplayBrightness,
+ * DisplayBrightnessSliderPosition alongside), and IOMFBBrightnessLevel on the
+ * framebuffer only once, 0 (the "1" in 1002's line was that line's count).
+ * The nits it pushes to CoreAnimation ("pushing nits to CA", -[CAWindowServer
+ * Display setNits:], NitsPhysical) are this table's value at B. 1002's
+ * table (2 + 498 B^2) gave 15 nits at the B it settled on (0.16; it fell
+ * from 0.46 at start, no light sensor): under CA's 20, so the luma boost
+ * stayed -- and under 30 CA also does its "display overdrive fix". The
+ * table is now a34blmin + (a34blmax - a34blmin) B^2 nits, by default 40..480
+ * (480: about this panel's normal maximum, DBV 0x3FF), so CA never sees
+ * less than 40. The same curve gives the panel its level (1004).
  */
 #define SWEET_FB_BL_MAX         65536u
-#define SWEET_FB_BL_NITS        500u
+#define SWEET_FB_BL_NITS_MIN    40u
